{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>וַיַּרְא אַהֲרֹן</b> — meaning, he saw a wondrous thing, for he did nothing but cast it into the fire, and the calf emerged on its own." "<b>וַיִּבֶן מִזְבֵּחַ לְפָנָיו</b> — and it does not say ״וַיִּבֶן לְפָנָיו מִזְבֵּחַ,״ for then it would be understood that he made it for its [the calf's] honor. Rather, he did not make the altar for the calf, but לְפָנָיו — before it — he made it, and his intention was toward the Place [i.e., HaShem]. And according to the words of the Zohar (vol. 2, p. 193a) it is also precisely directed, for he made it so that it [the altar] would not be visible outside, and the altar served him as a prison [maʾasar] for all those liable to the death penalty." "And he said <b>חַג לַה׳ מָחָר</b> — he intended to delay the hour, and his intention and thought in his words was toward the God of Israel in truth, for this Name is the designated Name, and 'Israel' too, according to what I have explained, for their thought and faith was not uprooted from HaShem, the true El, and toward Him they directed their intention — only that they wished to take a portion of Him that would be before them. There is nothing contrary to their mindset in the words of Aaron."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :register {:flags {2 ["God"]}}, :notes {1 "The phrase לְבַל יַפְלִיא חוּץ is understood as 'so that it would not be visible/distinguished outside'; מַאֲסָר read as a place of confinement for those subject to execution, per the Zohar's reading of Aaron's stratagem."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:35:39.057395702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}